# Copy to .env for LOCAL mode (no control plane at all: `cp .env.local
# .env`). Cedar policies are read straight from ./policies/ on disk --
# see README.md's "Switching between cloud and local mode". Nothing here
# needs a real agent_id/secret; this mode never makes a network call to
# the control plane.

PARAPETAI_MODE=local

# --- Model: mock by default -------------------------------------------
# Leave OPENAI_API_KEY unset (or "mock") to use the built-in local mock
# model server -- no network call, no cost, fully deterministic. Set a
# real key here to use a real OpenAI-compatible model instead; the agent
# code is identical either way.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=

# Nothing below this line is read in local mode -- ./policies/ is loaded
# directly instead. Left here, commented out, only so switching back with
# `cp .env.cloud .env` doesn't mean retyping real values.
# PARAPETAI_AGENT_ID=
# PARAPETAI_AGENT_SECRET=
# PARAPETAI_CONTROL_PLANE_URL=https://app.parapet.run
# PARAPETAI_ACCOUNT_ID=
